+# Desert close-up reference, original dust and wind-shaped banks
+
+2026-10-12 owner follow-up. DS11 restores original desert dust; DS12 restores driven directional sand; DS13 replaces detached/sharp banks with wind-shaped irregular deposits; DS14 removes two dominant material grooves; DS15 improves road/terrain readability; DS16 removes hard crossing/join edges; DS17 reduces colour contrast within the wear. Preserve V02/V04/V05/G01/R01/Q01, five laps, local car condition, approved tire-mark colour and canonical driving/scoring. AAA remains the requested visual standard with owner and device review open.
+
+Original desert cloud generation is restored: presentation 21, nine-second lifetime, 64 wake particles per wheel, original 4 m cards/growth/spread/damping/gravity/opacity/emission behavior and bridge protection. Initial restoration matched the historical source byte for byte. A concurrent winter task later adds snow-push behavior to the same file; those changes are retained. The final desert profile/cloud/alpha/growth/rotation/configuration/emitter functions are individually exact against the pre-refinement source, with hashes in `evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/original-desert-dust.json`. No final whole-file hash equality is claimed after the independent winter edits. Existing original-dust assertions are reinstated; directional daylight checks remain.
+
+The selected original artwork is smooth compacted sand with quiet longitudinal worn layers, following the later road-only crop. Earlier generated v1/v2 artwork is archived outside the export root. The shader normalizes the actual tile's pigment separately for Compatibility and Mobile, uses mipmaps/anisotropic sampling and a 0.75 mip bias, and limits the wear multiplier to roughly 0.90–1.08. There are no two deliberately strong full-length material lanes. Road pigment changes from `8d795b` to `7c6b51` for separation from the terrain. The decorative road/shoulder strip narrows from 1.47 m to 0.93 m; its actual interpolation occupies about 0.28 m. This is a textured join, not a broad fog overlay. Tire traces remain their existing independent presentation.
+
+Bank construction is now a nine-band rounded/asymmetric cross-section with a broad crest, spatially varying height, width, toe position, leaning crest, local erosion and low deposit gaps. Outer feet are buried and match the dune material. Small fragments sit on the actual crest rather than separate oval piles. Final fragments stay below 0.36 m; the previous 0.28 m diagnostic bound is explicitly revised for the reference-driven low-fragment design, with all road-clearance and buried-foot checks retained. The saved circuit has 6,287 accepted sections and 184 fragments (240 cap), approximately 101,880 bank triangles and 60,799 unique checked bank vertices after indexing. Banks/aprons stay in the existing shoulder batch with shadow casting. They are decorative; no collider, surface-cell or canonical force change is introduced.
+
+Ground crossings keep the preceding non-overlapping road union. Directional wear phase now follows connected road geometry, including reverse-authored sections and near-parallel overlapping free-placed joins, independently of the timed lap route. Closed connected loops fit whole texture periods. Bridge approaches receive the same phase data. Junction vertex colours encode a secondary road's periodic coordinates and its distance-weighted contribution; the shader blends both opaque worn surfaces over a bounded 2.5 m edge range. This prevents one direction's pattern ending abruptly at the ownership boundary. Boundary queries use six-metre spatial bins and cached points. The final reported owner crop's excessive wear contrast is reduced without lightening the road into the surrounding terrain.
+
+Runtime files: `game/track/native_track_visual.gd` (task presentation 174; later concurrent increments retained), `desert_sand_banks.gd`, `desert_road_union.gd`, `surface_detail.gdshaderinc`, `creator_road.gdshaderinc`, `track_theme.gd`, `creator_bridge_visual.gd`, `bridge_presentation.gd`, `desert_bridge_visual.gd`, `bridge_road.gdshaderinc`, and `game/vehicle/sand_dust.gd` (only the requested desert restoration). Selected asset/import: `game/assets/textures/desert_compacted_road_v3.png`. Tests: `test_desert.gd`, `test_bridge_dust.gd`, `test_desert_crossings.gd`, `capture_desert_refinement.gd`, new `profile_desert_reference.gd` (+UID). Documentation: this report, the prompt/provenance file, status, plan and agent override. Concurrent breakable/container/winter work is excluded from the task checkpoint.
+
+The material's source-colour handling follows the renderer distinction documented in [Godot spatial shaders](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/spatial_shader.html) and the texture hint guidance in [Godot shading language](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html). Actual tile measurements and both renderers' captures validate the implementation rather than relying on an assumed fixed pigment average.
+
+Actual commands use pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` via `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`:
+
+| Action / suffix | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_desert_refinement.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/final'` | Six final Compatibility views; 60,799 bank vertices checked for low height, buried feet and road clearance; cells/hash unchanged. |
+| Same with `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/mobile'` | Six final desktop Mobile/Vulkan views; same geometry/canonical checks. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_desert_crossings.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/crossing/'` | Final 77 checks, zero failures: reversed/closed wear continuity, exact single union coverage, junction blend data, 48 camera poses and four rendered ownership-edge samples. RGB motion delta 0.005546, below unchanged 0.025 threshold. |
+| Same with `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/mobile-crossing/'` | Final 77 checks, zero failures; RGB motion delta 0.0 and rendered edge checks pass. |
+| `TestDesert` | 87 checks, zero failures; original dense dust and exact five-car replay/packed-sand behavior. |
+| `TestShoulders` | Union plus 71 joins/18 contours pass; retained canonical contacts/cells. |
+| `TestRoadCache` | 70 checks, zero failures; restored meshes/materials/UV data. |
+| `TestBridgeContacts` | 16 checks, zero failures. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_bridge_dust.gd -Graphical` | Final 121 GPU/lifecycle checks, zero failures after shared class registration. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/profile_desert_reference.gd -Graphical` | 1600×900 RTX 3090, original dust and real unscored AI; 3 s warmup, 8 s measured, 1,937 frames/960 ticks/20.58 m movement. Frame median 3.933 ms, p95 5.714, maximum 18.685; GPU median 0.978, p95 1.675 ms. Desktop smoke sample, not old/new, sustained thermal or phone acceptance. |
+| `Import` | Final pass after registering concurrent classes. |
+| `Doctor` | Matching tools/templates; no attached Android devices. No phone test performed. |
+
+Initial iterations and actual failures are retained in logs. A fixed pigment reference saturated Compatibility into a flat road; measured renderer-specific pigment fixes it. Fine grain initially exceeded the unchanged crossing motion threshold (0.034412); mip filtering reduces it. A negative UV diagnostic initially misclassified valid connected-road UVs as banks; material-based bank selection fixes that while retaining clearance assertions. The initial timed-route phase attempt did not cover free-placed overlaps; connected geometry and local junction blending replace it. Repeated imports encountered concurrently introduced `BreakableProps`, `ContainerPaint` and `ContainerVisual` before class registration/file completion; final import and dust checks pass. Rejected sharp-bank/dominant-groove/strong-tone intermediate captures are kept under the evidence's earlier folders. The inherited biome-editor New-flow fixture failures were not rerun or claimed resolved. No full Validate/physics merge is claimed.
+
+Inspected final [driving view](evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/final/after/route-35.png), [detail](evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/final/after/bank-detail.png), [restored dust](evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/final/after/driving-dust.png), [Mobile view](evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/mobile/after/route-35.png) and [junction](evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/crossing/frame-00.png). Final crossing folders contain 24 rendered camera-pose images per renderer. Actual generation prompts and selected asset path: [provenance](DESERT_REFERENCE_PROMPTS_2026_10_12.md).
+
+Task-only baseline/fix Git checkpoint and patch: `build/desert_reference/checkpoint-repo`, `docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/task-only.patch`. Main branch/index and unrelated work remain preserved. No Android export/install, production deployment, backend operation or live account write. Remaining acceptance: owner reference/style review, representative multi-way/painted/elevated joins and physical-device readability/performance/thermal behavior. The saved capture track is not the owner's exact pictured track.
