+# Original desert road artwork provenance
+
+Built-in imagegen skill/tool, 2026-10-12. Owner crops are appearance references, not shipping assets. No runtime AI/API call is added. Fictional cars and the existing original dune/apron artwork remain.
+
+Selected shipping texture: `game/assets/textures/desert_compacted_road_v3.png`, imported at up to 1024 square with mipmaps and anisotropic sampling. Original output: `C:/Users/ville/.codex/generated_images/01a13084-3fd7-7892-9a1b-d856a6b75eea/exec-9e266731-d4b5-4357-9c8a-7bf5cdc795ff.png`. The generated source is copied unchanged; pigment, filtering, tile phase blending and direction along curves are shader/mesh code.
+
+Final generation prompt, verbatim:
+
+> Generate a NEW ORIGINAL square seamless game material texture, straight orthographic overhead albedo swatch, for a mature AAA-quality 3D desert racing road. The entire square is ONLY compacted dry sand that has been repeatedly driven on: mainly smooth matte worn sand with broad, layered shallow lengthwise abrasions and subtly lighter swept streaks; very fine sand grain, no visibly loose gravel. Many irregular delicate strands run TOP TO BOTTOM, softly meander and fade in and out, with a few extremely restrained slightly darker incomplete scuffs spread across the full width. Warm muted tan-brown compacted sand, naturally varied but with quiet low contrast and coherent longitudinal flow. Visual target: smooth compressed sand on a worn desert bend, where the broad sweeps and shallow worn layers read at game camera distance; not pebbly construction aggregate, not fluffy dune ripples, not a flat solid fill, not wood, not asphalt. No dominant two tyre lanes, no sharp full-height grooves, no heavy black marks, no hard stripes, no clouds or fog. The texture is flat-lit neutral diffuse albedo with no baked directional shadows or cast shadows, no gloss. No road edges, banks, vehicles, text or frame. The game maps these straight wear strands around its actual bends, so DO NOT bake a curved road composition into the swatch. Seamless/tileable on all edges, vertical streaks continue through top/bottom. Subtle and polished physically believable compacted sand.
+
+Earlier original generations are retained outside the export root under `docs/evidence/desert-reference-2026-10-12/generated-source/`. The v1 result had two overly dominant grooves. The v2 edit removed them, but remained too gravelly for the owner's later compacted-road crop; v3 is selected. They are not production acceptance evidence.
+
+V1 generation prompt, verbatim:
+
+> Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: original AAA quality game road albedo material texture, square 1024x1024 or higher. Generate ONLY a seamless tileable overhead orthographic material swatch of a well-driven compacted desert sand road. No scene, no road borders, no car, no text, no watermark, no bank, no dunes. Entire image is the drivable sand surface. Sand is matte muted warm tan/brown ochre (not grey, not bright yellow). Numerous subtle layered longitudinal abrasion grooves and shallow pressed wheel ruts run continuously from TOP TO BOTTOM, mostly straight but organically wavy; different widths, aged interrupted finer grooves, small swept sand grain streaks parallel to travel, occasional tiny embedded grains. A few softly worn darker wheel-path strands, NOT two stark tyre tracks or evenly spaced stripes. Rich physical small-scale detail and layered worked sand, with quiet broader pigment so it doesn't form blurry patches or fog. Strong coherent VERTICAL directionality at driving distance, believable eroded grain when zoomed in. Flat diffuse neutral illumination, no cast shadows or perspective, no sheen. Seamless edges both directions; vertical grooves continue perfectly through top and bottom. Production-ready original texture, mature restrained stylized realism suitable for a high-oblique 3D racer. The owner's supplied reference is guidance for the well-driven sand material, not an edit target; do not copy the road bank or curved composition.
+
+V2 targeted edit of v1, verbatim:
+
+> Edit target: the attached square game road material texture, preserving its warm muted compacted-sand colour, fine mineral grit, shallow directional abrasion and top-down flat diffuse material presentation. Single targeted correction: REMOVE the two prominent dark, uninterrupted vertical grooves and all similarly dominant full-height dark strands. Fill these dark lines with matching worked sand. Replace them with numerous low-contrast, shallow, irregularly interrupted vertical scuffs of varying widths, no paired tyre-track pattern and no groove spanning the whole tile. Keep readable subtle top-to-bottom traffic direction throughout, fine gritty texture and small weathered grains; do not blur it into fog or add broad patches. Seamless tileable material, no edges/road banks/text/objects/camera/lighting change. AAA game texture, quiet weathered physical surface rather than any two strong rails.
+
+V1 and v2 original output filenames in the same generation directory: `exec-3372de66-0e09-44f6-99b8-ebc49f9b67f5.png` and `exec-f6970023-482c-4e4a-a5ac-a2e75a8afe4c.png`. Saved unchanged under the evidence folder. No user-provided reference pixels are included in the selected asset.
